<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates plunge on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates plunge on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates plunged on Wednesday as demand from cash-short spinners faltered and dealers said prices could edge lower on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said prices could drop further due to the lack of funds among spinners and a build-up of about two million bales of unsold stocks at ginneries overhanging the market.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, NIAB-78 variety was traded at 2,100 rupees ($52.21) per maund (37.32 kg), dealers said.  </p>
<p>Wednesday's official spot rates issued by the Karachi Cotton Association in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>					   Wednesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    NIAB-78 (1996/97 crop)	 2,355.50	   2,383.00</p>
<p>    K-68    (1996/97 crop)	 2,559.00	   2,575.50</p>
<p>    MNH-93  (1996/97 crop)	 2,569.00	   2,585.50</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
